@startuml payment-sequence
!include style.iuml
hide footbox
autonumber

actor "Customer\napp" as App
participant "DashCart API" as API
database "MySQL" as DB
participant "Razorpay" as RZP

App -> API : POST /orders/{id}/payment
API -> DB : order still holding stock\nand not expired?
API -> RZP : POST /v1/orders (amount in paise,\nreceipt), Basic auth key id : secret
RZP --> API : order_id
API -> DB : INSERT payments (CREATED);\norder → PAYMENT_PENDING
API --> App : 201 (razorpayOrderId, amount, keyId, payBefore)
App -> RZP : Razorpay Checkout: customer pays (UPI / card)
RZP --> App : payment_id, signature
par browser confirms
  App -> API : POST /payments/razorpay/verify
  API -> DB : SELECT payment ... FOR UPDATE
  API -> API : HMAC-SHA256(order_id | payment_id,\nkey secret) == signature ?
  API -> DB : capture: order → PAID (conditional),\nconfirm stock, payment CAPTURED
  API --> App : 200 (payment CAPTURED)
else Razorpay confirms
  RZP -> API : POST /payments/razorpay/webhook\n(payment.captured, signed raw body)
  API -> API : HMAC-SHA256(raw body,\nwebhook secret) == signature ?
  API -> DB : INSERT webhook_events (provider, event_id)\nduplicate event id → ignored
  API -> DB : SELECT payment ... FOR UPDATE;\ncapture (no-op if already CAPTURED)
  API --> RZP : 200 OK
end
note over API, DB
  Whichever arrives first captures the payment; the second finds it CAPTURED and does nothing.
  If the order expired first, the payment becomes REFUND_REQUIRED instead.
end note
@enduml
